def has_pair(nums, target):
    seen = set()
    for x in nums:
        if target - x in seen:
            return True
        seen.add(x)
    return False

The function passes through the list once. Set membership and insertion are O(1) on average because sets are hash tables, so the total is O(n). Checking x before adding it ensures an element is never paired with itself. Checking every pair with nested loops would be O(n²).

